    <bpmn:process id="W_W3238" name="W3238. Technology Refresh, Replacement Cycle &amp; Rollout" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Lifecycle/end-of-support; performance/obsolescence; security/vulnerability (W3250); new capability
Frequency: Annual plan + project waves
Volume: ~3–5 year refresh cycles; ~600 POS + ~2,500 endpoints
Owner: IT Asset Manager
Participants: IT Asset Mgr, IT Ops (links to VS-27), Finance (links to VS-40/VS-35), Procurement (links to VS-34), Store Ops
Source: workflow W3238 — Technology Refresh, Replacement Cycle &amp; Rollout</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3238_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3238_Lane1" name="IT Asset Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3238_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3238_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3238_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3238_Lane2" name="IT Ops">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3238_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3238_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3238_Start4" name="Lifecycle/end-of-support; performance/obsolescence; security/vulnerability (W3250); new…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3238_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3238_Task5" name="IT Asset Mgr/Finance build refresh plan: device lifecycle policy by class (POS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: IT Asset Mgr/Finance build refresh plan: device lifecycle policy by class (POS 5–7 yr, laptop 3–4 yr, server 4–5 yr, network 5–7 yr), vendor end-of-support dates (W3250), performance/TCO analysis (W3251), capex budget (links to VS-40); prioritize by risk and ROI
Responsible (R): IT Asset Mgr / Finance
Accountable (A): IT Asset Manager
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3238_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3238_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3238_Task6" name="Execute refresh wave: procure (W3234), provision/deploy (W3235) with minimal…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Execute refresh wave: procure (W3234), provision/deploy (W3235) with minimal operational disruption (after-hours, phased by region), recover and retire old devices (W3239) — recovered devices re-custody to the IT Asset Manager&#x27;s spare pool as a release-and-accept event on the asset register&#x27;s Assigned-To field (links to VS-35 W1693), update CMDB and fixed assets (links to VS-35); manage trade-in/resale value
Responsible (R): IT Ops / Field IT / Procurement
Accountable (A): IT Ops Manager
Duration: Per wave</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3238_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3238_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3238_Task7" name="Manage disposal accounting (links to VS-35.3): derecognize retired assets…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manage disposal accounting (links to VS-35.3): derecognize retired assets, gain/loss on disposal, transfer to new assets; capture lessons and update refresh policy; report refresh KPI (cycle adherence, residual value)
Responsible (R): IT Asset Mgr / Finance
Accountable (A): IT Asset Manager
Duration: Per wave</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3238_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3238_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3238_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3238_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3238_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-526 (ensure controlled execution — IT Hardware Asset Lifecycle &amp; Deployment (PA-99.1).) | - operational: lifecycle policy and budget; operational: after-hours/phased rollout
Owner: IT Asset Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
