    <bpmn:process id="W_W3239" name="W3239. Asset Retirement, Data Sanitization &amp; E-Waste Disposal" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Refresh (W3238); damage beyond repair; lease return; site closure (links to VS-59)
Frequency: Continuous + project waves
Volume: Hundreds–thousands of retirements/year
Owner: IT Asset Manager
Participants: IT Asset Mgr, Security (links to VS-27.3/VS-91), Finance (links to VS-35), Sustainability (links to VS-73/VS-25), Disposal Vendor
Source: workflow W3239 — Asset Retirement, Data Sanitization &amp; E-Waste Disposal</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3239_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3239_Lane1" name="IT Asset Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3239_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3239_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3239_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3239_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3239_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3239_Start3" name="Refresh (W3238); damage beyond repair; lease return; site closure (links to VS-59)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3239_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3239_Task4" name="IT Asset Mgr/Security retire devices: revoke access/deactivate (MDM, AD, apps…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: IT Asset Mgr/Security retire devices: revoke access/deactivate (MDM, AD, apps per VS-27.3), perform certified data sanitization (NIST 800-88 / cryptographic erase for SSDs) to ensure no residual BuildRight or customer data (Data Privacy Act RA 10173 compliance, links to VS-91); document sanitization certificate per asset
Responsible (R): IT Asset Mgr / Security
Accountable (A): IT Asset Manager
Duration: Per asset</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3239_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3239_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3239_Task5" name="Decide disposition: redeploy internally (cascade to lower-tier use), resell…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Decide disposition: redeploy internally (cascade to lower-tier use), resell (trade-in, secondary market — recover value), donate (CSR per VS-25, with sanitization), recycle/dispose as e-waste (DENR-accredited treatment/storage/disposal — TSD facility per VS-73.2 hazardous/e-waste compliance); ensure no data-bearing media leaves unsanitized
Responsible (R): IT Asset Mgr / Sustainability
Accountable (A): IT Asset Manager
Duration: Per asset</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3239_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3239_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3239_Task6" name="Reconcile retirement: derecognize from CMDB (W3233) and fixed assets (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Reconcile retirement: derecognize from CMDB (W3233) and fixed assets (links to VS-35.3), record gain/loss/disposal cost, retain sanitization/disposal certificates (links to VS-88) for audit and privacy compliance (links to VS-91); report e-waste and recovery metrics to sustainability (links to VS-25/VS-73)
Responsible (R): IT Asset Mgr / Finance
Accountable (A): IT Asset Manager
Duration: Per asset</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3239_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3239_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3239_End7" name="Complete">
